# Shared wiki workflow

- Shared memory lives in `../ai-development-wiki` (private repo `Freedomfarms/ai-development-wiki`).
- Before changing code, run `scripts/cloud-agent-wiki.sh check`. On `WARNING`, say the wiki is
  unavailable and do not claim shared memory was loaded; fall back to `README.md` and `docs/`.
- When available, read `index.md` and `log.md` at the wiki root, then `wiki/projects/freedom-os/`,
  `wiki/projects/forward-freedom-financial/`, and the shared standards under `wiki/shared/` first.
- Wiki updates go through pull requests in `ai-development-wiki` only. Never push to its `main`,
  never copy wiki content into this repo, and never commit credentials for it.
- On every pull request, run `node scripts/wiki-sync.mjs classify` (same command Codex uses; do not
  start a second agent for documentation impact). Follow the marker contract in `AGENTS.md`.
  A `no-update-required` marker cannot waive a `wiki-required` result. If wiki write access is
  unavailable, the documentation-sync check fails closed. Owner authorization is a merge by the
  repository owner, recorded by the GitHub API, of that exact wiki head into the default branch.
  Another user's Approve review on that head also qualifies. A sentence in the pull request body
  is not authorization.
- Full setup and troubleshooting: `docs/SHARED_WIKI.md`.
